---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PlaceholderImage from '../components/PlaceholderImage.astro';
import PullQuote from '../components/PullQuote.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Teaching"
  description="Why I want to teach ceramics, my teaching philosophy, and the kind of studio I hope to help build."
  active="teaching"
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 pt-14 sm:px-8 sm:pt-20">
    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl text-ink sm:text-5xl">Teaching</h1>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 1 — Why I Want to Teach -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-14 sm:px-8 sm:py-20">
    <div class="grid gap-10 sm:grid-cols-2 sm:items-center sm:gap-14">
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl text-ink">Why I Want to Teach</h2>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-measure text-base leading-relaxed text-clay sm:text-lg">
          When I first started throwing, I wasn't naturally good at it. Centering felt
          impossible, my pieces collapsed, and I questioned whether I would ever improve. What
          kept me coming back wasn't quick success&mdash;it was instructors who encouraged
          experimentation, celebrated small wins, and made the studio feel like a place I
          belonged. Years later, I still carry those lessons with me, and they're a big part of
          why I want to teach.
        </p>
      </div>
      <PlaceholderImage
        alt="Studio photograph of a wheel-thrown piece early in the process, still uneven"
        ratio="aspect-[4/5]"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 2 — My Teaching Philosophy -->
  <section class="border-t border-mist/40 bg-mist-50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-14 sm:px-8 sm:py-20">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl text-ink">My Teaching Philosophy</h2>

      <div class="mt-8 grid gap-10 sm:grid-cols-2 sm:gap-14">
        <p class="max-w-measure leading-relaxed text-clay">
          Every student learns differently. Some students want detailed demonstrations before
          they begin, while others learn best by getting their hands dirty and asking questions
          along the way. My goal is to understand how each student learns and meet them where
          they are.
        </p>
        <p class="max-w-measure leading-relaxed text-clay">
          I've experienced both sides of that dynamic myself. I've been the advanced student in
          beginner classes who needed very little guidance, and I've also been the least
          experienced student in intermediate classes who benefited from extra encouragement and
          one-on-one support. Those experiences taught me that great instruction isn't
          one-size-fits-all.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- The contrast the brief asks to emphasize, handled typographically
           rather than with a heavier graphic treatment: two words set in
           the display italic, divided by a thin oxblood rule. -->
      <div class="mt-12 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 font-display text-xl italic text-ink sm:text-2xl">
        <span>technical foundations</span>
        <span class="h-px w-10 bg-oxblood sm:w-14" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>room to explore</span>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-8 max-w-measure leading-relaxed text-clay">
        I believe the best classes balance technical foundations with room to explore. Students
        should leave understanding <em class="not-italic font-medium text-ink">why</em> a technique
        works while also feeling excited to experiment and develop their own creative voice.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 3 — The Kind of Studio I Hope to Build -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-14 sm:px-8 sm:py-20">
    <div class="grid gap-10 sm:grid-cols-2 sm:items-center sm:gap-14">
      <PlaceholderImage
        alt="Wide studio photograph showing several students working at wheels together"
        ratio="aspect-[4/5] sm:order-2"
        class="sm:order-2"
      />
      <div class="sm:order-1">
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl text-ink">The Kind of Studio I Hope to Build</h2>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-measure leading-relaxed text-clay">
          Community is one of the reasons I fell in love with ceramics.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-measure leading-relaxed text-clay">
          Having worked in community studios across San Francisco, Boston, and New York, I've
          seen how much an instructor shapes the culture of a class. The best instructors didn't
          just teach throwing&mdash;they remembered students' names, encouraged conversations,
          celebrated progress, and created spaces where people wanted to spend time together.
        </p>
        <PullQuote class="mt-8">
          I'd love to help build that kind of environment at Firebox: one where students feel
          welcomed, supported, and excited to return each week.
        </PullQuote>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
